  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Dissect MS-TURN 0x0004 as Send Request",
  "description": "MS-TURN uses STUN message type `0x0004` for Send Request, which does not align with the standard RFC 5389 message type encoding (see [section 2.1.1 of MS-TURN](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/office_protocols/ms-turn/8177788b-1f38-47a5-8a6f-348e89717922)). Currently, MS-TURN messages with header type `0x0004` are interpreted as Refresh Request. This patch fixes that.\n\nBuilding on the fix that was merged a few months ago (https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/23814), this patch adds two MS-TURN-specific message types: `MS_TURN_SEND` and `MS_TURN_DATA_IND`. When the first attribute is a valid MAGIC_COOKIE, the dissector reinterprets the message type as MS-TURN.",
  "state": "merged",
